    {
      "source": "Doctors of Running",
      "priority": 3,
      "url": "https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2025/07/adidas-adizero-prime-x3-strung-review.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The 50 mm heel / 43 mm forefoot Lightstrike Pro setup gives very high impact protection with a soft, highly cushioned ride at the heel, while the forefoot feels more firm/stiff and needs break-in.",
        "Responsiveness: Energy return is strongest at the heel with pronounced bounce, and the plate + Energy Rods + rocker create a quick, snappy heel-to-forefoot roll (especially for rearfoot strikers).",
        "Stability: Torsional rigidity is very high (the shoe is essentially non-flexible), but midfoot stability is reduced versus the prior version; heel lockdown is decent via collar padding despite no heel counter, and lateral support is best only on stable, even surfaces.",
        "Durability: Outsole durability looks above average with no visible wear after 35+ miles and good material longevity so far, though there is a noted concern about possible wear/separation risk around the split midfoot outsole."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Road Trail Run",
      "priority": 4,
      "url": "https://www.roadtrailrun.com/2025/07/adidas-adizero-prime-x3-initial-review.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: Extremely deep max cushioning (50 mm heel / 43 mm forefoot) feels soft, dynamic, and highly forgiving, with strong impact protection and a smoother heel-to-forefoot roll than prior versions.",
        "Responsiveness: Energy return is strong and consistent from the plate + EnergyRods setup, giving solid forefoot impulse and smooth toe-off, but bounce/flight feels less explosive than earlier Prime X models.",
        "Stability: Major stability improvement from the wider midfoot/forefoot platform and revised geometry/plating, with secure heel-midfoot lockdown, better torsional control, and reliable lateral tracking across paces.",
        "Durability: New mostly Traxxion outsole (with a small Continental forefoot piece) is described as a lighter material with a good durability reputation, but long-term wear is not yet confirmed from the short test period."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Believe in the Run",
      "priority": 5,
      "url": "https://believeintherun.com/shoe-reviews/adidas-prime-x3-strung-review/",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The 50 mm heel / 43 mm forefoot stack and three-density Lightstrike Pro create a plush, highly protective ride, with softer foam underfoot, firmer foam at the perimeter, and smoother long-run comfort than the X2’s harsher feel.",
        "Responsiveness: The shoe keeps a springy, trampoline-like character, and the single full-length carbon plate plus Energy Rods 2.0 improve toe-off snap and turnover; Lightstrike Pro is described as very resilient with strong energy return.",
        "Stability: A tighter Strung upper and sock-like collar improve lockdown, while firmer outer-side foam and the plate/rods setup add structure, though the very tall platform can still feel somewhat bottom-heavy.",
        "Durability: The Continental + Lighttraxion outsole is specifically called out for added durability and grip, with no early outsole-wear issues mentioned in the review."
      ]
    }
